From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sluongng <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj: Read default index roots without mutation

Native-object collection needs every indexed commit at every retained
operation, including hidden commits not present in a view. The ordinary
index loader may build missing associations or reinitialize a corrupt
index, so it cannot serve as an observational collection prerequisite.

Expose an opt-in reader of explicit operation associations and their
commit-segment chains. Return all indexed IDs rather than only graph
heads: index parent relationships need not independently prove canonical
object reachability. Verify content hashes, the pinned version-six
layout, lookup coverage and topological references before returning
any roots.  Only the actual intrinsic root operation may omit its
association, in which case the caller-supplied intrinsic root commit
is retained.

Reuse compact, validated shared segments only within one observation.
Retained operations otherwise rescan the same history quadratically.
Read every association again and start a fresh memo for each independent
observation; retain all indexed IDs rather than weakening root coverage.
Bound live allocations separately from cumulative I/O and validation
work.  Use non-owning parent links so custom deep chains also have
shallow cleanup.

Bound file reads, control decoding, chain depth, aggregate
observations, returned roots and conservative working allocations before
growth. Share validated compact segments only within one inventory call,
while reading every operation control and giving each independent
observation a fresh memo. Retain only local IDs and generations,
never raw payloads or growing full-prefix sets; separately bound
validation steps and current live bytes.  Never initialize, repair,
delete or invoke a backend. Callers still own trusted path validation
and mutation/collection fencing. Optional changed-path cache payloads
do not contribute commit roots and are not loaded. Existing index
loading behavior and all on-disk formats remain unchanged.

---
